288 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 217 0 R
/E (Campus food services often experience long waiting times, uneven customer distribution across canteens, inaccurate demand estimation, and inefficient order management, leading to student inconvenience, food wastage, and increased operational burden. Traditional food ordering systems primarily focus on digital payments and online ordering but lack intelligent mechanisms for real-time congestion management, demand prediction, and decentralized decision-making. EATALY addresses these challenges through a decentralized campus food management ecosystem that integrates load-aware routing, capacity-bounded scheduling, and on-device demand forecasting to optimize food ordering and distribution across multiple campus canteens. The proposed system consists of a student mobile application, an administrative dashboard, and a cloud-based backend that work together to provide seamless order placement, real-time queue monitoring, and efficient kitchen management. EATALY dynamically recommends the least congested canteen using a load-balancing algorithm, allocates pickup slots based on kitchen capacity, and employs lightweight machine learning models to forecast food demand from historical ordering patterns and temporal trends. The platform also incorporates inventory monitoring, digital token generation, secure user authentication, multilingual support, and offline synchronization to ensure reliable operation even under intermittent network connectivity. A user-centric interface designed through the Design Thinking methodology enhances accessibility and simplifies interactions for students, faculty, and canteen administrators. The proposed architecture is scalable, modular, and suitable for deployment across educational institutions with multiple food outlets. By intelligently distributing customer demand, minimizing queue congestion, improving resource utilization, and enabling data-driven operational decisions, EATALY aims to transform conventional campus dining into a smart, efficient, and sustainable food management ecosystem while significantly enhancing the overall user experience.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
