/P 221 0 R
/E (The increasing adoption of digital technologies has transformed various services within educational institutions, including food ordering and campus management. However, many college canteens continue to rely on conventional ordering methods or basic online systems that primarily support menu browsing and payment processing. These systems often lack intelligent mechanisms to manage customer flow, predict food demand, or optimize kitchen operations, resulting in congestion during peak hours and inefficient utilization of available resources.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
374 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 221 0 R
/E (Campus food services play a vital role in supporting the daily activities of students, faculty members, and staff within educational institutions. However, managing food ordering and distribution efficiently remains a significant challenge due to increasing student populations, limited serving capacity, and concentrated demand during peak hours. Conventional canteen operations primarily rely on manual ordering, physical queues, or basic digital ordering systems, which often lead to prolonged waiting times, uneven customer distribution, inaccurate demand estimation, and inefficient utilization of kitchen resources.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
