/E (Managing food services in educational institutions is challenging due to increasing student populations, limited serving capacity, and concentrated demand during break and lunch hours. Conventional canteen operations often lead to long waiting queues, uneven customer distribution, inaccurate demand estimation, and inefficient kitchen scheduling. Existing digital ordering systems primarily focus on order placement and payment processing, offering limited support for congestion management, resource optimization, and operational planning.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
380 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 222 0 R
/E (Eataly aims to address these issues by developing a centralized food ordering and cafeteria management application that connects students with campus cafeteria services. The application enables students to browse menus, view food item details and prices, place orders digitally, and track their order status. By reducing dependence on manual ordering and improving access to information, the system seeks to enhance the overall food ordering experience.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
