/P 232 0 R
/E (The primary requirement of EATALY is to provide an integrated digital platform that simplifies campus food ordering while improving operational efficiency for canteen administrators. The system must support user authentication, menu management, online food ordering, secure payment processing, real-time order tracking, and notification services. It should also facilitate communication between students, kitchen staff, and administrators through a centralized cloud infrastructure. In addition to these functional requirements, the system should provide intelligent features such as load-aware canteen recommendation, capacity-based pickup scheduling, demand forecasting, and administrative analytics. Non-functional requirements include reliability, scalability, security, usability, and real-time performance to ensure seamless operation across multiple campus food outlets and a consistent user experience.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
446 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 232 0 R
/E (System design defines the overall architecture, components, and communication flow required for developing an intelligent campus food management ecosystem. EATALY consists of three interconnected components: the student mobile application, the administrative dashboard, and a cloud-based backend infrastructure. The student application enables users to browse menus, place food orders, make digital payments, and receive real-time order updates. The administrative dashboard allows canteen staff to manage menus, monitor orders, analyze sales, and oversee daily operations. The cloud backend synchronizes data between all system components while supporting secure authentication, real-time database updates, and intelligent decision-making. Features such as load-aware canteen recommendation, capacity-based pickup scheduling, and demand forecasting work together to optimize food service operations, improve resource utilization, and enhance the overall campus dining experience. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
