/E (The experimental evaluation of EATALY was carried out using the developed Flutter mobile application, Firebase backend services, and the Staff Administration Portal. The system was deployed on Android smartphones connected to the same cloud database, enabling real-time synchronization between student users and canteen staff. Simulated order requests were generated from multiple student accounts while staff members processed these requests through the administration portal to evaluate live communication and system responsiveness.)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
624 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 256 0 R
/E (Testing and evaluation were conducted to assess the functionality, reliability, and overall performance of the EATALY smart campus food management system. The evaluation focused on validating core features such as user authentication, menu browsing, smart load balancing, digital token generation, pickup slot allocation, crowd prediction, bilingual interface, and live order tracking. Both the Student Portal and Staff Portal were tested to ensure seamless communication and synchronization between users and canteen administrators.)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
625 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 256 0 R
/E (Functional testing was performed for every module to verify that orders were correctly processed, digital tokens were generated without duplication, and real-time status updates were reflected accurately across both portals. The crowd prediction and smart load balancing features were evaluated using simulated peak-hour ordering scenarios to confirm that the system successfully recommended alternative canteens with lower waiting times. In addition, usability testing was conducted with multiple users to evaluate interface responsiveness, ease of navigation, and bilingual language support, ensuring a smooth user experience across different devices.)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
626 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 257 0 R
/E (The EATALY system was evaluated using multiple real-world campus dining scenarios to verify the performance of its smart food ordering, crowd management, and staff coordination features. Testing covered student ordering, slot booking, kitchen workflow, live order tracking, bilingual interface switching, and staff dashboard operations under different demand conditions.Different crowd levels were simulated by varying the number of active users and orders across multiple campus canteens. The system monitored waiting times, kitchen workload, pickup slot availability, and order routing decisions. Live synchronization between the student application and staff portal was verified to ensure that every order status update was reflected instantly for both students and administrators.)
/Pg 52 0 R
/K [0]
>>
