651 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 261 0 R
/E (The major achievement of EATALY is the successful integration of intelligent queue management and real-time cloud-based services into a single mobile platform. The application supports secure user authentication, menu browsing, online ordering, digital token generation, smart load balancing, crowd visualization, pickup slot scheduling, multilingual staff communication, and real-time notifications through Firebase. The proposed algorithms effectively distribute customer traffic across available counters, reducing congestion and improving service efficiency. Performance testing demonstrated reliable synchronization between the mobile application and cloud database, validating the practicality of the system for handling day-to-day cafeteria operations. The modular architecture also provides flexibility for future enhancements, including AI-based demand prediction, IoT integration, and advanced analytics for canteen management.)
/Pg 56 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
652 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 261 0 R
/E (EATALY successfully demonstrates the development of a smart canteen management system that integrates mobile technology, cloud computing, and intelligent scheduling algorithms to improve the overall food ordering experience. The system combines a Flutter-based mobile application with Firebase services to provide real-time order processing, secure authentication, cloud synchronization, and digital token management. Features such as smart load balancing, crowd heatmap visualization, pickup slot booking, bilingual staff management, and instant notifications help reduce waiting time, optimize queue distribution, and improve operational efficiency. Experimental testing confirmed that the proposed system performs reliably under different ordering scenarios, providing a scalable, user-friendly, and efficient solution for modern educational institutions and workplace cafeterias.)
/Pg 56 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
653 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 262 0 R
/E (Although EATALY functions as a fully operational prototype, its evaluation was conducted primarily using simulated cafeteria data and controlled testing environments. The performance of features such as smart load balancing and crowd prediction depends on the accuracy of real-time user activity and order information. Network latency, internet connectivity, and sudden surges in customer demand may influence synchronization and response time during peak hours. Furthermore, the current implementation does not incorporate IoT-based occupancy sensors or advanced AI models for demand forecasting, limiting the precision of crowd estimation in highly dynamic environments. Additional large-scale deployment across multiple cafeterias is required to comprehensively evaluate system scalability, reliability, and long-term performance.)
/Pg 57 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
654 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 262 0 R
/E (Future development of EATALY can focus on improving intelligence, scalability, and user convenience. Machine learning models can be integrated to predict food demand, optimize inventory management, and provide personalized meal recommendations based on user preferences. IoT-based occupancy sensors and computer vision techniques can further enhance crowd estimation and improve the accuracy of smart load balancing. The application can also support multiple campus cafeterias, digital wallet integration, loyalty and reward programs, nutritional analysis, and voice-assisted ordering. Administrative dashboards with advanced analytics and reporting can assist canteen managers in monitoring sales, peak-hour trends, and operational efficiency. These enhancements would transform EATALY into a comprehensive smart cafeteria management platform suitable for educational institutions, corporate campuses, and large-scale food service environments.)
/Pg 57 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
